SUMMARY:LET THERE BE LIGHT
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:USA | 1946 | DCP | 58 min.\n\nDirector: John Huston\n\nSuppres
 sed and unseen for decades\, Huston’s powerful documentary chronicles t
 he rehabilitation of psychologically traumatized World War II veterans\, 
 revealing the human cost of war with uncommon empathy. Presented in conju
 nction with the exhibition Craft/Work: A History of Occupational and Art 
 Therapies\, open in the Ebling Library Historical Reading Room from Septe
 mber 8 through December 17.\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/events/let-there-b
 e-light/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/let-there-be-light/
END:VEVENT
