UID:cinematheque-2816-0-1794014100@cinema.wisc.edu
DTSTAMP:20261107T011500Z
DTSTART:20261107T011500Z
DTEND:20261107T025200Z
SUMMARY:BRIGHT VICTORY
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:USA | 1951 | 35mm | 97 min.\n\nDirector: Mark Robson\n\nCast: 
 Arthur Kennedy\, James Edwards\, Peggy Dow\n\nAfter he gets blinded by a 
 German sniper’s bullet in 1943\, Sergeant Larry Nevins (Kennedy\, in an
  Oscar-nominated lead performance) begins the long and painful road to re
 covery. Landing in a military hospital\, Larry pursues a romance with att
 ending nurse Judy (Dow)\, while his casual racism affects his growing fri
 endship with an African-American soldier\, Joe (Edwards). This powerful\,
  somewhat neglected postwar drama about a veteran’s redemption through 
 courage and love will be screened in an excellent 35mm archival print. Pr
 esented in conjunction with the exhibition Craft/Work: A History of Occup
 ational and Art Therapies\, open in the Ebling Library Historical Reading
  Room from September 8 through December 17.\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/ev
 ents/bright-victory/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/bright-victory/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cinematheque-2817-0-1794099600@cinema.wisc.edu
DTSTAMP:20261108T010000Z
DTSTART:20261108T010000Z
DTEND:20261108T023800Z
SUMMARY:JOSIE AND THE PUSSYCATS
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:USA | 2001 | 35mm | 98 min.\n\nDirector: Harry Elfont\, Debora
 h Kaplan\n\nCast: Rachael Leigh Cook\, Rosario Dawson\, Parker Posey\n\nW
 hen an evil record label implants subliminal messaging in pop music to br
 ainwash the youth\, rock trio Josie and the Pussycats become their unwitt
 ing Trojan Horse. Josie’s buoyant spoof of consumerism gamely extends t
 he gag to the film itself\, which is an unparalleled parody of product pl
 acement. Simultaneously subversive and escapist\, this underrated comedy 
 features a memorable batch of mall-punk cuts by alt-rock ringers like Ada
 m Schlesinger. (MK)\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/events/josie-and-the-pussy
 cats/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/josie-and-the-pussycats/
END:VEVENT
