SUMMARY:CHRONOVISOR
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:USA | DCP | 2026 | 100 min. | French\, English\, German\, and 
 Italian with English subtitles\n\nDirector: Kevin Walker\, Jack Auen\n\nC
 ast: Anne-Laure Sellier\n\nIn the 1960s\, an Italian Benedictine monk cla
 imed to have invented a machine that allowed users to see into the past\,
  as though on a TV set. While doing research\, present-day academic Béat
 rice becomes fascinated by this “Chronovisor\,” and plunges headlong 
 into uncovering the truth about this mysterious device. This unusual and 
 beguiling indie perfectly captures the sensation of going down a rabbit h
 ole of dubious arcana. (MK)\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/events/chronovisor
 /\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/chronovisor/
