SUMMARY:PARAMOUNT ON PARADE
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:USA | 1930 | 35mm | 102 min.\n\nDirector: Ernst Lubitsch\, Edm
 und Goulding\, Dorothy Arzner and 8 others\n\nCast: Gary Cooper\, Clara B
 ow\, Fredric March\n\nA great burst of pre-code fun\, Paramount on Parade
  was Paramount Pictures’ contribution to the all-star studio musical re
 vue movie cycle of the early talkie years. Featuring 20 individual segmen
 ts from 11 directors\, the movie is literally a showcase for the incredib
 le talents under contract: Gary Cooper\, Clara Bow\, Fredric March\, Maur
 ice Chavalier\, Jean Arthur\, Kay Francis\, Jack Oakie\, William Powell\,
  Fay Wray\, and lots\, lots more stars. Hard to see for many years\, a fe
 w sequences have been lost or partially lost. This 35mm preservation prin
 t courtesy the UCLA Film & Television Archive restores the two-color Tech
 nicolor to several sequences and is the most complete version available. 
 35mm restored print courtesy of the UCLA Film & Television Archive.\n\nht
 tps://cinema.wisc.edu/events/paramount-on-parade/\n\nSource: UW Cinemathe
 que
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/paramount-on-parade/
END:VEVENT
