SUMMARY:MICHAEL MANN’S MANHUNTER: THE FINAL CUT
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:USA | 1986 | DCP | 120 min.\n\nDirector: Michael Mann\n\nCast:
  William Petersen\, Brian Cox\, Tom Noonan\n\nBefore Jonathan Demme’s T
 he Silence of the Lambs\, writer/director Michael Mann first brought Thom
 as Harris’ popular series of crime novels to the screen with this allur
 ing adaptation of Red Dragon. Retreating to a quiet life with his family 
 after taking down the infamous Hannibal Lecktor (Cox)\, FBI “manhunter
 ” Will Graham (Petersen) returns to work following the emergence of an 
 enigmatic new killer. An extraordinarily stylish modern thriller\, Manhun
 ter is an immersive portrait of Graham’s obsessive pursuit. Mann has de
 clared this new 4K restoration to be the final\, definitive version of hi
 s landmark procedural. (JM)\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/events/michael-man
 ns-manhunter-the-final-cut/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/michael-manns-manhunter-the-final-cut/
END:VEVENT
