DTSTAMP:20261205T000000Z
DTSTART:20261205T000000Z
DTEND:20261205T013500Z
SUMMARY:SALESMAN
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:USA | 1969 | DCP | 95 min.\n\nDirector: David Maysles\, Albert
  Maysles\, Charlotte Zwerin\n\nA landmark American documentary from the t
 eam that later made Grey Gardens and Gimme Shelter\, Salesman marks a hig
 hpoint in 1960s cinema verité. Aging door-to-door Bible salesman Paul Br
 ennan is followed through his struggles with sales quotas and the somber 
 desperation and frustrations of constant travel. As a study of business a
 nd religion\, materialism and spiritualism\, few non-fiction movies speak
  with such sensitivity and subtle beauty.\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/even
 ts/salesman/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/salesman/
END:VEVENT
