SUMMARY:UNDER THE SKIN
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:UK\, USA\, Switzerland | 2013 | DCP | 108 min.\n\nDirector: Jo
 nathan Glazer\n\nCast: Scarlett Johansson\, Jeremy McWilliams\, Adam Pear
 son\n\nIn this one-of-a-kind cinematic odyssey from director Jonathan Gla
 zer (The Zone of Interest\, Birth)\, an alien creature takes the form of 
 a woman (Scarlett Johansson) in contemporary Scotland. As this malevolent
  visitor prowls the streets\, various men fall victim to its tantalizing 
 disguise\, yet life as a human soon takes its toll. Guided by a disquieti
 ng musical score from composer Mica Levi\, Glazer’s horrific sci-fi tal
 e features shades of the rigorous formal style employed by Stanley Kubric
 k. Audaciously experimental\, Under the Skin is one of the most acclaimed
  films of the twenty-first century thus far. (JM)\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.
 edu/events/under-the-skin/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/under-the-skin/
END:VEVENT
