SUMMARY:THE DREAMLIFE OF ANGELS
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:France | 1998 | 35mm | 113 min. | French with English subtitle
 s\n\nDirector: Erick Zonca\n\nCast: Élodie Bouchez\, Natacha Régnier\, 
 Gregoire Colin\n\nStars Bouchez and Régnier shared the Best Actress priz
 e at the Cannes Film Festival for their raw\, deeply compassionate portra
 its of two young women who develop a friendship on the margins of contemp
 orary France. Refusing easy clichés about youth\, the film follows their
  diverging paths with honesty\, capturing both the exhilaration of possib
 ility and the compromises demanded by adulthood. Screening in a rare 35mm
  print courtesy of the Wisconsin Center for Film & Theater Research\, Dre
 amlife remains one of the great discoveries of 1990s French cinema.\n\nht
 tps://cinema.wisc.edu/events/the-dreamlife-of-angels/\n\nSource: UW Cinem
 atheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/the-dreamlife-of-angels/
END:VEVENT
