SUMMARY:ALL OF A SUDDEN
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque
DESCRIPTION:France\, Japan\, Germany\, Belgium | 2026 | DCP | 196 min. | F
 rench and Japanese with English subtitles\n\nDirector: Ryûsuke Hamaguchi
 \n\nCast: Virginie Efira\, Tao Okamoto\, Kyozo Nagatsuka\n\nThe director 
 of a Parisian nursing home and a Japanese theater director form a close p
 ersonal bond in this profoundly humane exploration of the struggle for di
 gnity in the face of capitalist society. Oscar-winning director Ryusuke H
 amaguchi’s French-language debut introduces fascinating new dimensions 
 to his acclaimed body of work\, especially through the quietly soulful le
 ad performances of Virginie Efira and Tao Okamoto\, who shared the Best A
 ctress prize at Cannes. “Radically tender and enriching… crystallizes
  into something that can change your understanding of what’s possible o
 n screen and off” (Sight & Sound). (MK)\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/even
 ts/all-of-a-sudden/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/all-of-a-sudden/
END:VEVENT
