SUMMARY:12 MONKEYS
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:USA | 1995 | 35mm | 129 min.\n\nDirector: Terry Gilliam\n\nCas
 t: Bruce Willis\, Brad Pitt\, Madeleine Stowe\n\nWillis stars as a haples
 s “volunteer” from the future\, sent to 20th century Baltimore by the
  post-apocalyptic-powers-that-be to try and figure out who or what trigge
 red a pandemic that killed 99% of the earth’s human population. Directo
 r Gilliam’s Hollywood-blockbuster riff on Chris Marker’s La Jetee tee
 ms with details that bring to life his visions of a dystopian future and 
 the almost-as-dystopian present. 12 Monkeys masterfully combines mordant 
 humor\, surreal lunacy\, big screen sci-fi action set pieces\, and an ach
 ingly vulnerable\, melancholic heart. (BR)\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/eve
 nts/12-monkeys/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/12-monkeys/
END:VEVENT
