DTEND:20261212T230800Z
SUMMARY:FANNY AND ALEXANDER
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:Sweden | 1982 | 35mm | 188 min. | Swedish with English subtitl
 es\n\nDirector: Ingmar Bergman\n\nCast: Pernilla Allwin\, Bertil Guve\, J
 an Malmsjö\n\nAt the twilight of his illustrious career\, Bergman mined 
 his own childhood memories for this moving family drama told on a grand s
 cale. When the patriarch of the Ekdahls\, a Swedish family of actors in t
 he early twentieth century\, dies suddenly\, the children (Allwin and Guv
 e) must adjust to life under Bishop Edvard (Malmsjö)\, their mother’s 
 cruel new husband. Bergman’s austere mood and signature existential med
 itations here exist in tandem with moments of warmth and joy\, including 
 an extended sequence chronicling the family’s annual Christmas party. A
  35mm print of the film’s theatrical version will be screened. (JM)\n\n
 https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/fanny-and-alexander/\n\nSource: UW Cinemat
 heque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/fanny-and-alexander/
END:VEVENT
