SUMMARY:BLUE
LOCATION:Chazen Museum of Art\, 750 University Ave\, Madison\, WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:UK | 1993 | 35mm | 76 min.\n\nDirector: Derek Jarman\n\nCast: 
 Nigel Terry\, Derek Jarman\, Tilda Swinton\n\nCreated as he was dying of 
 AIDS and losing his sight\, Derek Jarman’s powerful final film famously
  consists of a single image: a screen-filling shade of blue. Blue’s vis
 ual monochrome is contrasted with a richly layered soundscape\, as Jarman
  weaves a poetic account of his life as a gay man in London and impending
  mortality alongside contributions from longtime collaborators like Tilda
  Swinton and music by artists including Brian Eno and Coil. This singular
  cinematic experience will only be enhanced by screening on a 35mm print 
 from the film’s original release. (MK)\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/event
 s/blue/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/blue/
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
